@* Help — the boundary, stated plainly, and the route out.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Reachable from the nav, and directly from every refusal, failed gate check
   and no-cache error state in the app: the person who most needs the boundary
   spelled out is the one who just hit it, not the one browsing a menu.

   Entirely static, and that is a requirement rather than a convenience. The
   offline path through this app terminates here, so this page has to be
   readable with no signal at all. Nothing on it fetches anything. *@

@page "/help"

<PageTitle>Help</PageTitle>

<h1>Help</h1>

<p class="help__intro">
    This app shows what your accreditation currently permits, what has changed
    about it, and why. It is not the accreditation system itself, and it cannot
    change any decision that system has taken.
</p>

<section class="help__section">
    <h2>Where you are in the process</h2>

    <h3>Before you apply</h3>
    <p>
        Nothing appears here until an application exists against your credential
        number. Applications are made through your member association, your
        broadcaster, or the freelance route — not through this app.
    </p>

    <h3>While your application is being assessed</h3>
    <p>
        This is the longest silence in the whole process, and this app cannot
        shorten it. There are no interim stages to report during assessment, so
        an empty record here means your application has not yet reached a
        decision — not that it has been overlooked.
    </p>

    <h3>Once a decision is taken</h3>
    <p>
        The decision appears as a change, with the reason attached and whatever
        you can do next. Approval is always stated as approved <em>until</em> a
        date, because it is never open-ended.
    </p>

    <h3>During the tournament</h3>
    <p>
        Your access can move after approval — quotas contract, zone lists get
        revised, and some entitlements depend on results that have not happened
        yet. Every one of those movements is written here before it takes
        effect, so you find out by reading rather than by being turned away.
    </p>

    <h3>On a matchday</h3>
    <p>
        The state on this screen is the last one your device managed to fetch,
        and it always shows its own age. Check that age before you rely on it.
        If the venue's list disagrees with what you see, this app records the
        disagreement and points you at a person — it does not settle it.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="help__section">
    <h2>What this service does not do</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Visas and entry permissions.</strong> Nothing here affects your right to enter any host country, and this app does not know your visa status.</li>
        <li><strong>Vetting outcomes.</strong> Security vetting is carried out elsewhere and its reasoning is not shared with this app.</li>
        <li><strong>Quota decisions.</strong> How many places your association or broadcaster receives, and who gets them, is decided outside this app entirely.</li>
        <li><strong>Guaranteed access.</strong> Nothing shown here is a promise. An entitlement recorded today can be changed tomorrow, which is exactly why the record exists.</li>
        <li><strong>Appeals.</strong> There is no appeal channel in this app, and the section below is not one.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="help__section">
    <h2>What will not reach you as a notification</h2>
    <p>
        Some changes are written to your record without interrupting you. They
        are still there to read; they simply do not raise an alert. If they did,
        the alerts that matter would be buried among them.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Corrections to administrative details that do not affect what you can do.</li>
        <li>Documents you re-uploaded being accepted.</li>
        <li>Access being <em>widened</em> — a zone or a match added rather than removed.</li>
        <li>Your existing state being re-confirmed without changing.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        This list is published for one reason: an unexplained silence is
        indistinguishable from a broken app. If nothing has reached you, you
        should be able to check here and know why.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="help__section">
    <h2>Who to contact</h2>
    <p>
        This app does not accept submissions, and sending something here would
        not reach anyone. Contact the people who already hold your file:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Your member association or broadcaster media officer</strong> — for anything about quota, allocation, or which of your colleagues holds which place.</li>
        <li><strong>The accreditation centre in the host city</strong> — for a credential that will not scan, a lost pass, or a disagreement at a barrier.</li>
        <li><strong>FIFA Event Media Operations</strong> — for a decision you believe was recorded against the wrong person or the wrong match.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="help__mocked">
        Contact routes are described here in general terms. This version of the
        app is a demonstration and carries no live contact details or
        integrations.
    </p>
</section>
